{
  "dom_id": "step-q143103",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "A wireless headphone set includes $2$ earbuds (left and right) and a charging case.\nThe weights of the earbuds are normally distributed with mean $4\\,\\text{g}$ and a variance of $0.01\\,{\\text{g}}^{2},$ while the weights of charging cases are normally distributed with mean $38\\,\\text{g}$ and a variance of $0.14\\,{\\text{g}}^{2}.$\n\n If one headphone set is randomly selected, what is the probability that it weighs less than $45.8\\,\\text{g}?$ You may assume that the weights are independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2119\\,$ | $\\,0.2090\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ | $\\,0.2033\\,$ | $\\,0.2005\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.2420\\,$ | $\\,0.2389\\,$ | $\\,0.2358\\,$ | $\\,0.2327\\,$ | $\\,0.2296\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.2743\\,$ | $\\,0.2709\\,$ | $\\,0.2676\\,$ | $\\,0.2643\\,$ | $\\,0.2611\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.3085\\,$ | $\\,0.3050\\,$ | $\\,0.3015\\,$ | $\\,0.2981\\,$ | $\\,0.2946\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Let ${X}_{1}$, ${X}_{2},$ and ${X}_{3}$ denote the weight of the charging case, and the weights of the left and right earbuds, respectively. Then, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}∼N(38,0.14),\\,{X}_{2}∼N(4,0.01),\\,{X}_{3}∼N(4,0.01).\n$$\n\nLet the random variable $Y$ denote the weight of the headphone set. Then, we have\n\n$$\nY={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+{X}_{3}.\n$$\n\nThe random variable $Y$ is normally distributed, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & =38+2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =46, \\\\ \\text{Var}[Y] & =0.14+0.01+0.01 \\\\  & =0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nY∼N(46,0.16).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $P(Y<45.8),$ we convert $Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<45.8) & =P(Z<\\frac{45.8-46}{\\sqrt{0.16}}) \\\\  & =P(Z<-0.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.5)≈0.3085.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<45.8) & =Φ(-0.5) \\\\  & =0.3085.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
